  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Bilal Naveed, holder of account PK**BAHL****1230, opened on 28 October 2023. The customer's declared occupation is medical sales officer (salaried), with a declared income of PKR 185,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 1 August 2026 to 30 August 2026, the account recorded 17 credits totalling PKR 25,830,000 as well as 6 debits totalling PKR 22,676,000. The credits included 16 cash deposits totalling PKR 25,645,000, made over the counter at 4 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch). The activity was detected on 30 August 2026, when Tazama typology STR-PK-01 scored 320 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: 12 of 16 cash deposits (75%) were between PKR 1,600,000 and PKR 1,999,999, totalling PKR 22,418,000, just below the cash transaction reporting threshold of PKR 2,000,000. The cash was deposited across 4 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch) rather than at a single branch. The customer made more than one cash deposit on 1 day (9 August 2026). Credits in the activity window were 139.6 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 185,000 per month. A note by Branch Operations (14 August 2026): "Customer asked why deposits of PKR 2 million or more need extra paperwork and declined to explain the source of the cash." Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected structuring; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 9,344,000 was sent to Crescent Imports (PK**CRES****1592, Synthetic Bank B) in 2 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 8,165,000 was sent to Al-Noor Exchange Company (PK**AL-N****1888, Synthetic Bank B) in 2 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 5,167,000 was sent to Sheraz Traders (PK**SHER****1518, Synthetic Bank C) in 2 transactions. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 88% of credits, with a median of 3.8 hours between the latest credit and each debit.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 28 August 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (28 August 2026): "Account placed under enhanced monitoring pending the reporting decision. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
